            Digital Completes the Most Expansive Line of
          Windows NT Optimized Servers with Two New Models


      New Prioris Servers provide big-business performance and
                 features on a small-business budget


MAYNARD, Mass., Feb. 3, 1997 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
rounded out its award-winning Prioris Pentium Pro processor server 
line today with the introduction of two new entry-priced server 
series.  Priced significantly below similar competitive products, 
the new DIGITAL Prioris XL 6000 series entry-level and DIGITAL 
Prioris MX 6200 departmental servers are ideal for Microsoft Windows 
NT Server deployment of Inter/intranet, mail and messaging, and 
business applications as well as for file/print and shared-resource 
services.

     "With todays introduction, DIGITAL provides the most expansive 
line of Windows NT optimized servers in the industry," said Bruce 
Claflin, vice president and general manager of DIGITAL's Personal 
Computer Business Unit.  "As the first enterprise systems vendor to 
bring Windows NT optimized Pentium Pro processor-based systems to 
the entry-level segment of the server market, DIGITAL again leads 
the way with its enterprise solutions," he added.

     The company also introduced a 19-inch rackmount enclosure, 
which is designed to support the complete DIGITAL Prioris line; 
Revision Manager, a new DIGITAL ServerWORKS Quick Launch feature; 
and support for Tivolis TME 10 NetView.

     "The new DIGITAL Prioris servers offer customers best-in-class 
award-winning enterprise features and price/performance leadership 
in the Windows NT market," said Howard Elias, vice president, 
worldwide business segments for DIGITAL's PC Business.

Easily Managed with ServerWORKS

     Included with the new Prioris XL 6200 and Prioris MX 6200 
systems -- at no extra cost -- is DIGITAL ServerWORKS Manager, an 
easy-to-use software package that extends the capabilities of 
traditional server management to provide critical network management 
functionality.  Also included with the systems is ServerWORKS Quick 
Launch, an installation and configuration utility designed to save 
customers hours of installation by auto-replicating customized 
server configurations in distributed computing environments.

     DIGITAL also introduced today DIGITAL ServerWORKS Quick Launch 
Revision Manager.  The optional CD-ROM subscription service allows 
channel partners and LAN administrators at large end-user customer 
sites to manage software updates and provides them with a complete 
revision history of system software and driver updates.

     DIGITAL also announced new advances in enterprise management 
integration resulting from Tivoli Systems agreement to assume 
development of the POLYCENTER NetView enterprise management product.  
DIGITAL's ServerWORKS Manager product now features tight integration 
with TME 10 NetView allowing customers to retrieve detailed data on 
their DIGITAL Prioris and DIGITAL Alpha servers from within the TME 
management environment.  Customers can "snap in" ServerWORKS Manager 
software into their TME 10 NetView management console allowing them 
to perform queries and set alarms directly from the console.

     "This tight integration is consistent with Tivolis approach of 
working with partners to provide benefits customers can touch and 
feel," said Chris Grafft, senior vice-president of business 
development at Tivoli Systems.

     In addition, the Prioris MX 6200 series includes DIGITAL's 
Intelligent Server Management for proactive monitoring of critical 
subsystems, such as CPUs, RAID, fans, power supplies and memory 
based on the company's innovative design and use of inter-integrated 
circuit technology to provide system administrators with up-to-the 
minute status and alerting.  The Prioris MX also includes optional 
support for Remote Server Manager, the company's out-of-band system 
management for remote sites or "lights-out" environments.

High Availability and Reliability

     Because uptime is essential in businesses of any size, DIGITAL 
includes industry-leading features and options from its high-end 
Prioris servers in today's new systems for total enterprise 
solutions which meet the most demanding customer needs.  Hardware 
features, such as DIGITAL-designed motherboards, ECC memory, RAID 
support and hot swappable device shelves protect data and minimize 
downtime.  All DIGITAL Prioris Pentium Pro processor-based systems 
support DIGITAL Clusters for Windows NT, a layered software 
application, which allows for the clustering of two DIGITAL Prioris 
or Alpha servers.  With more than 50 percent of the market for 
Windows NT clustered solutions shipped in calendar year 1996, 
DIGITAL is the recognized leader.

Performance Pro

     Priced at Pentium processor-based levels, the new systems come 
with a number of high-end features for value and investment 
protection.  Both lines incorporate 200 MHz Pentium Pro processors 
with 256KB on-chip cache with double the performance of equivalent 
Pentium processor-based systems in Windows NT application 
environments.  Other standard features include an integrated 
Ultra/Wide SCSI controller, PCI Fast 10/100 Ethernet controller, and 
12X SCSI CD-ROM drive.  Available in single and dual processor 
configurations, the Prioris MX 6200 supports up to 1 GB of ECC 
memory, integrated 32-bit graphics and hot-pluggable drives.

     "We are pleased that DIGITAL is bringing Intel Pentium Pro 
processor technology to the entry-level server segment," said Tom 
Macdonald, director of Marketing, Enterprise Server Group, Intel 
Corporation.  "Paired with the Pentium Pro processor, the DIGITAL 
Prioris server line provides an excellent server platform for small- 
and medium-size businesses."

Investment Longevity

     All DIGITAL Prioris servers are fully optimized to meet 
customers needs today and in the future.  Designed for growth, the 
new Prioris XL 6000 series has five available I/O slots and up to 
nine drive bays -- four in an easy-access swing-out drive cage.  The 
Prioris MX 6200 server comes with seven available I/O slots and 
eight drive bays -- four are hot swappable.  To help customers 
realize a return on their information technology investment, the 
DIGITAL Prioris line is also upgradeable to future higher-speed 
processors.

     DIGITAL also introduced today a space-saving, easy-to-install 
rackmount enclosure.  The secure, 81-inch tower supports up to eight 
DIGITAL Prioris servers.  Customers can rackmount existing DIGITAL 
Prioris enclosures without modification through the use of flexible 
assembly options.

Services

     DIGITAL's complete line of PC servers is backed by an industry-
leading three-year on-site warranty, with next-business-day response 
standard from authorized DIGITAL Warranty Service Providers and 
DIGITAL's Multivendor Customer Services organization.  In addition, 
the company offers a number of services packages, including the 
DIGITAL Priority Service Plan, which provides a set of packaged 
services -- Priority, Priority-Plus, and Priority-Premier -- 
designed to meet availability requirements for a wide range of 
customers.

Pricing and Availability

     The new Prioris servers are available this month.  U.S. 
estimated street prices start in the mid $2,000 range for a typical 
configuration of the DIGITAL Prioris XL 6000 series, based on 
configuration.  For a typical configuration of the DIGITAL Prioris 
MX 6200 servers, U.S. estimated street prices begin in the mid 
$3,000 range, depending on the configuration.  The DIGITAL Prioris 
Rackmount estimated street price starts at US $2,000.  DIGITAL 
ServerWORKS Quick Launch Revision Manager is available at a nominal 
charge for shipping, handling and media.  All of DIGITAL's Prioris 
servers are available through DIGITAL's channel partners, including 
master resellers, wholesalers, distributors, dealers, VARs and system 
integrators.  For complete pricing information, please refer to the 
DIGITAL Prioris server fact sheets or call 1-800-DIGITAL.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha and Intel platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
