      Digital and TransAlta Sign $70 Million Services Contract


    ...Seven-year Pact Expands and Extends Previous Agreement...


CALGARY, February 24, 1997 -- Digital Equipment Corporation and 
TransAlta Corporation, an energy management company doing business 
in Canada and internationally, today announced the signing of a 
major, multi-million dollar information services contract.  It will 
help TransAlta achieve a 15 to 20 per cent reduction in operational 
and systems support costs over the next seven years.

     The new agreement, estimated at $70 million (U.S.), marks an 
expansion of an earlier, five-year relationship with DIGITAL that 
began in July 1992.

     APPROXIMATELY 100 DIGITAL employees are on-site providing 
services that range from help desk and on-site end user support, SAP 
data center maintenance and support, system management, Lotus Notes 
support, and voice and data network management for more than 2,500 
users.

     DIGITAL and a TransAlta systems team have implemented a new 
integrated communications infrastructure, enabling TransAlta to 
share information effectively between its many offices and 
departments.  The SAP R/3 applications running on Alpha-based 
systems are some of the first in the electric utilities industry.

     DIGITAL has also managed the move from a DIGITAL VAX systems 
platform to a Microsoft Windows NT and Windows 95 desktop and server 
computing environment.  "We needed a technology partner that not 
only understood information technology but the unique demands of our 
industry," said Gary Moore, vice president of information technology 
services at TransAlta.  "As deregulation brings about increased 
competition, TransAlta is challenged to provide top-notch customer 
service at reduced operating costs.  DIGITAL solutions help us do 
that."

     "The DIGITAL experience in global markets supports TransAlta's 
growth strategy," added Moore.  "We are expanding successfully into 
new markets at home and abroad, and a solid information services 
infrastructure is key to our success."

     Andy Akrouche, vice president, DIGITAL Operations Management 
Services in Canada said: "TransAlta need a highly responsive team to 
provide its vital service.  We are delivering comprehensive 
technology migration and management services across mutlivendor 
systems, network, and applications."

     Headquartered in Calgary, Alberta, TransAlta Corporation has 
annual sales in excess of $1.6 billion.  The corporation operates 
through two main subsidiaries -- TransAlta Utilities and TransAlta 
Energy.  Established in 1911, TransAlta Utilities owns and operates 
large-scale generation, transmission and electricity distribution 
facilities throughout Alberta.  TransAlta Energy owns and operates 
three cogeneration plants in Ontario, has interests in a 1,400 
megawatt hydroelectric facility in Argentina, a cogeneration plant 
in Auckland, New Zealand, a power station in Parkeston, Western 
Australia and a distribution company in Wellington, New Zealand. The 
corporation also owns Canada's largest cogeneration plant in 
northern Albert.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems.  DIGITAL's scalable Alpha and Intel platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.  In addition to offices 
across Canada, Digital Equipment of Canada Limited has a major 
manufacturing facility in Kanata, Ontario, and a major service and 
support centre in Hull, Quebec.
